      <processInformation>
        <referenceFunction amount="1.0" category="material, obsolete" datasetRelatesToProduct="true" generalComment="In- and outputs are calculated for rare earth oxide processing with sulphuric acid as used in China. Infrastructure approximated with a chemical plant. Some inputs of auxiliary materials are calculated according to stoechiometry. Rough estimation for energy consumption, solvent use and waste generation.;&#10;UUID: 6bf7d4d4-b53e-3801-bb23-ebc61e7b1e38" includedProcesses="The process includes raw materials, processing chemicals and processing energy, emissions to water and wastes. Transport and infrastructure are estimated. The multi output-process &quot;rare earth oxide production from bastnasite&quot; delivers the co-products &quot;cerium concentrate, 60% cerium oxide, at plant&quot;, &quot;lanthanum oxide, at plant&quot;, &quot;neodymium oxide, at plant&quot;,&quot;praseodymium oxide, at plant&quot;, &quot;samarium europium gadolinium concentrate 94% rare earth oxide, at plant&quot;. The revenue is used as allocation scheme." infrastructureProcess="false" localCategory="material, obsolete" localName="xx Praseodymium oxide, at plant" localSubCategory="chemicals, obsolete\inorganic, obsolete" name="xx Praseodymium oxide, at plant" subCategory="chemicals, obsolete\inorganic, obsolete" unit="kg"/>
        <geography location="CN" text="&lt;null&gt;"/>
        <technology text="Process includes roasting and cracking of the rare earth concentrate with 98% sulphuric acid at 500°C in a rotary kiln. For the following separation of the different rare earth oxides solvent extraction (SX) is used. The obtained rare earth oxide product has a purity of up to 99.9%."/>
